remaining
 
concern
 
is
 
that
 
a
 
backup
 
can
 
also
 
be
 
lost,
 
outdated,
 
or
 
corrupted
 
if
 
it
 
is
 
not
 
stored
 
and
 
tested
 
properly.
 
 
 
 
 

Conclusion:  
 
In  conclusion,  the  activity  showed  that  confidentiality,  integrity,  and  availability  are  all  
important
 
for
 
protecting
 
student
 
grades.
 
Encryption
 
protects
 
confidentiality
 
by
 
preventing
 
unauthorized
 
users
 
from
 
reading
 
the
 
file.
 
A
 
normal
 
checksum
 
can
 
detect
 
changes,
 
but
 
it
 
is
 
weak
 
because
 
an
 
attacker
 
can
 
regenerate
 
it
 
after
 
tampering.
 
HMAC
 
provides
 
stronger
 
integrity
 
protection
 
because
 
a
 
valid
 
tag
 
requires
 
a
 
secret
 
key.
 
Finally,
 
backups
 
protect
 
availability
 
by
 
allowing
 
damaged
 
or
 
deleted
 
data
 
to
 
be
 
restored.'
